@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+# H200 Slurm benchmark launchers
+
+These launchers target this checkout and the cluster inspected on 2026-09-21.
+Submit from the Mooncake repository root, or export an absolute `MOONCAKE_ROOT`.
+They run existing workloads without changing benchmark implementations.
+
+## Workload inventory
+
+The repository has `benchmarks/`, not a top-level `benchmark/` directory.
+
+| Location | Workload and measurement |
+| --- | --- |
+| `benchmarks/storage_benchmark_v1` | Replays conversation, synthetic, and tool-agent JSONL traces from `FAST25-release/traces`. Repeated cache-page hashes drive reads; new pages drive writes. GLM-5 and Kimi-K2.6 MLA layouts determine object bytes. Measures QPS, hit rate, request wall/I/O latency, page-read/write bandwidth and percentiles. Supports replay pacing, multiple independent clients, single-file/per-page files, and fsync policies. This tests filesystem storage, not the Mooncake Store service. |
+| `benchmarks/xypd_benchmarks` | End-to-end vLLM disaggregated prefill/decode through MooncakeStoreConnector and a proxy. The shell demo sweeps 1P1D, 2P1D, 2P2D, 2P4D, 4P4D routing; random prompts of 1024/4096 input and 6/256 output tokens; concurrency 1/4/8/16 (1 only for 1P1D); 50-token prefix by default. Reports serving throughput and TTFT, TPOT, inter-token and end-to-end latency. It launches four prefill and four decode instances even for smaller routing configurations. |
+| `mooncake-store/benchmarks/store_kv_bench.py` | Real Store API workloads: verified writes, fill, write/read performance, mixed existing-object reads plus new-object writes; also metadata smoke/mix, remove performance, and recorded-operation replay in the current source. Plain and registered-buffer APIs; single/batch operations; worker/depth controls. Outputs request/KV rate, MiB/s, latency percentiles, misses/errors, JSON summary and journal. |
+| `allocation_strategy_bench` | Simulated allocation placement across segment/replica/strategy matrices: fill-up, scale-out convergence, DSA churn, weighted size-class churn. Measures allocation latency, throughput, utilization, partial/failing allocations and fragmentation. Virtual segment capacity is not physical cluster RAM. |
+| `allocator_bench`, `offset_allocator_concurrency_bench` | Low-level allocation patterns and concurrent allocator/PutStart stages; allocation/free cost and contention. |
+| `master_bench`, `batch_get_replica_bench` | Master metadata RPC throughput and batched replica-lookup latency, including dataset prefill and optional concurrent refill. Mounted segments are synthetic; these are not data-transfer bandwidth benchmarks. |
+| `storage_backend_bench` | Offset-allocator, bucket and file-per-key storage: initialization, offload, load, concurrent reads, existence, mixed reads/writes, churn and restart. Configurable object/batch sizes, key access patterns and cache modes; integrity checking. |
+| `file_interface_bench`, `uring_batch_read_bench` | File read/write bandwidth through POSIX/io_uring/direct-I/O variants; sequential versus batched aligned io_uring reads. Requires a build/kernel supporting the selected variant. |
+| `batch_evict_bench`, `batch_oplog_promotion_bench` | In-process eviction scale/mutex contention and synthetic standby object promotion in chunks. |
+| `batch_remove_benchmark.py` | Batch-remove API demonstrations, correctness checks and single/batch removal comparisons. Use `store_kv_bench.py --scenario remove_perf` for the supplied Slurm removal workflow. |
+| `oplog_batch_bench`, `run_oplog_batch_sweep.py`, `report_oplog_batch.py` | Etcd-backed operation-log batching: batch size, producer count, writer/backend throughput and latency; repeatable sweep and report tooling. Requires `STORE_USE_ETCD` and a dedicated etcd endpoint. |
+| `nof_worker_pool_bench` | SPDK NVMe-oF read/write/mixed I/O, sequential/random offsets, queue depth, request sizes, submission concurrency and endpoint scaling. Requires `USE_NOF` and configured storage targets. |
+
+The Slurm scripts cover local Store KV, the listed supported C++ microbenchmarks,
+and filesystem trace replay. They do not provision vLLM models/servers, etcd or
+NVMe-oF targets. The upstream vLLM demo installs packages and manages processes
+by ports; it is not used as an unattended Slurm entry point here.
+
+## Observed cluster
+
+- Cluster `slurm`, Slurm 25.05.3; account `cw-sup`, allowed QoS `normal`.
+- `h200`: **one** node, `slurm-h200-205-005`, eight H200 GPUs.
+- `h100`: two nodes; not used by these launchers.
+- Each node advertises 128 logical CPUs (64 cores, two sockets) and 2,031,616 MiB
+  RAM (1,984 GiB), with 32,768 MiB reserved by Slurm.
+- Default partition is `hpc-mid`. Other shared partitions are `all`, `hpc-low`,
+  `hpc-high`, and `hpc-prod`; scripts explicitly select `h200`.
+- H200 probe found local XFS at `/tmp`; `/mnt/home` is shared NFS. RDMA device
+  names include `ibp0` through `ibp7` and `mlx5_0` through `mlx5_8`. No bandwidth
+  or link-speed claim was measured.
+- At inspection the H200 node had five GPUs, 80 CPUs, and 500 GiB allocated.
+  Availability changes; jobs queue normally.
+
+Defaults request one node, one task, 16 CPUs/64 GiB for Store or 4 CPUs/16 GiB
+for trace replay, with a 30-minute limit. These are host-memory and disk tests:
+selecting H200 places them on that host but does not reserve or use a GPU.
+For isolated measurements add `--exclusive` (which may wait for other jobs).
+One H200 node cannot measure cross-node RDMA; KV defaults to local TCP with one
+memory replica. The single-process Store client owns its segment, so this can
+exercise local-copy paths and must not be labeled network throughput.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+The inspected environment has Python 3 but no Mooncake build directory,
+`mooncake_master` on PATH, or importable `mooncake` Python package. Build this
+checkout with the dependencies in `docs/source/getting_started/build.md`, and
+install its matching Python bindings in a shared environment. No system package
+installation is performed by these scripts.
+
+For an already provisioned build environment, enable benchmark targets:
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B build -DWITH_STORE=ON -DBUILD_BENCHMARK=ON
+cmake --build build --parallel 16 --target mooncake_master allocation_strategy_bench \
+  offset_allocator_concurrency_bench storage_backend_bench master_bench \
+  batch_get_replica_bench allocator_bench batch_evict_bench \
+  batch_oplog_promotion_bench file_interface_bench uring_batch_read_bench
+```
+
+Use `BUILD_DIR` for a different absolute build directory, `MASTER_BIN` for a
+master executable elsewhere, and `VENV_DIR` or `PYTHON` for Python bindings built
+from this revision. A generic released wheel may lack APIs in this checkout.
+Trace replay uses the standard Python library and does not require Mooncake.
+
+## Submit
+
+From the Mooncake repository root:
+
+```bash
+# Count-bounded, read-after-write verification: 1024 x 128 KiB, batches of 16.
+sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_kv.sbatch
+
+# Read performance with automatic dataset preparation and registered buffers.
+SCENARIO=read_perf IO_API=zcopy RUNTIME=30 \
+  sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_kv.sbatch
+
+# Existing-object reads and new-object writes, 70% reads by default.
+SCENARIO=mixed_rw sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_kv.sbatch
+
+SCENARIO=remove_perf sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_kv.sbatch
+
+# Allocation churn is the default microbenchmark.
+sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_micro.sbatch
+BENCHMARK=master_bench sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_micro.sbatch \
+  --operation=BatchGet
+BENCHMARK=batch_get_replica_bench \
+  sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_micro.sbatch
+BENCHMARK=storage_backend_bench \
+  sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/store_micro.sbatch \
+  --backend=all --test=mixed_rw --pattern=zipf
+
+# A bounded trace sample; choose each trace or all.
+SCENARIO=all sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/storage_trace.sbatch
+FSYNC_MODE=always MAX_REQUESTS=1000 MAX_PAGES=512 \
+  sbatch mooncake-store/benchmarks/slurm/storage_trace.sbatch
+```
+
+Arguments after the script path pass through to the benchmark; for C++ flags,
+later arguments override launcher defaults. Slurm options belong before the
+script path. Do not override service endpoints or output paths unless you also
+adapt the worker's readiness/summary handling. An existing replay journal can
+be supplied with `SCENARIO=replay` and `--replay-file /absolute/path`.
+
+| Launcher | Environment controls (defaults) |
+| --- | --- |
+| All | `MOONCAKE_ROOT` (submission directory), `BUILD_DIR` (`$MOONCAKE_ROOT/build`), `PYTHON` (`python3`), optional `VENV_DIR`, `RESULT_ROOT` (`$MOONCAKE_ROOT/benchmark-results`), `SCRATCH_ROOT` (`$SLURM_TMPDIR` or `/tmp`), `KEEP_SCRATCH` (`0`) |
+| Store KV | `SCENARIO=verify_write`, `IO_API=plain`, `OBJECTS=1024`, `WRITE_OBJECTS=1024`, `VALUE_BYTES=131072`, `BATCH_SIZE=16`, `NUMJOBS=4`, `IODEPTH=1`, `RUNTIME=0`, `SEGMENT_BYTES=8589934592`, `BUFFER_BYTES=268435456` |
+| Micro | `BENCHMARK=allocation_strategy_bench`; supported choices are the ten C++ targets in the build command above, excluding `mooncake_master` |
+| Trace | `SCENARIO=toolagent`, `TRACE_DIR` (`$MOONCAKE_ROOT/FAST25-release/traces`), `MODEL=glm5`, `THREADS=1`, `MAX_PAGES=128`, `MAX_REQUESTS=100`, `FILE_MODE=single`, `FSYNC_MODE=none`, `REPLAY_SCALES=0` |
+
+## Results and interpretation
+
+`benchmark-results/JOBID/` contains `benchmark.log`, host/filesystem details,
+Slurm allocation details, commit and worktree status. Service-backed jobs also
+save `master.log`; KV jobs save `kv/summary.json` and a journal; replica lookup
+saves `replica.csv`. Commands and resolved arguments are recorded in the log.
+The Slurm output file is created in the submission directory. Each job uses a
+unique scratch directory and shuts down only its own master process on exit.
+`KEEP_SCRATCH=1` retains data at the path recorded in `host.txt`.
+
+Verification/pattern generation, Python threads and service/client CPU sharing
+contribute to the measured cost. Write workloads are count-bounded by default;
+raise counts/runtime and segment size deliberately for capacity/eviction tests.
+KV summaries with `ok=false` fail the job even when the upstream performance
+scenario exits zero. Inspect misses, error counts and latency sample rate before
+comparing results.
+
+Trace defaults are smoke-scale, not a full trace reproduction. GLM-5 at 512
+tokens uses roughly 53.6 MiB per page, so 128 pages take about 6.7 GiB per client.
+Each extra thread replays a full independent trace and uses its own storage.
+If pages exceed the cap, modulo mapping reuses physical slots. `fsync=none`
+measures page-cache-backed I/O, not durable disk throughput. Per-file `batch`
+and `end` fsync modes have weaker durability than single-file mode; see the
+upstream trace README. No global cache dropping is performed.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `bash -n` separately on each `.sh` and `.sbatch` file. `sbatch --test-only`
+checks scheduling without submitting a job. Full Store execution requires the
+matching binaries/bindings described above. GPU-memory, multi-node RDMA,
+NVMe-oF and etcd-backed tests need additional topology/services and are outside
+these single-node launchers.
+
+Validation performed on 2026-09-21:
+
+- Shell syntax checks passed for every launcher and helper.
+- `sbatch --test-only` accepted all three requests on `slurm-h200-205-005`.
+- Job 1592 ran trace replay on H200 with one request and two physical pages;
+  Slurm reported `COMPLETED`, exit `0:0`. It wrote 14 logical pages using modulo
+  mapping and removed its scratch directory. This is a launch smoke test, not
+  a performance baseline.
+- Temporary stand-in master/benchmark executables verified successful and failed
+  benchmark exits (0 and 17), master termination and scratch cleanup.
+- Whitespace checks passed. `pre-commit` is not installed in this environment.
+- Real Store binaries/bindings were unavailable, so Store execution remains
+  unverified; no Store performance results are claimed.
